Review findings and fixes applied
-----------------------------------------------------------------
1. R6 verbatim check: re-read the LIVE 8c rejection predicate
   (rev6 lines 563-596) and compared row-by-row with the embedded R6
   diff block - exact logical complements on all five rows
   (is_deleted / status / impact_level / start_time / completion_time
   with matched strictness and NULL semantics). No predicate change.
   Nuance documented at 8g: b.is_deleted is not in the INSERT-eligible
   predicate; a deliberate raw insert with is_deleted = 1 produces an
   ack that 8c rejects and rolls back the whole insert - intentional
   fail-fast (R3).
2. Trigger SQL deep check: multi-row safety is set-based by
   construction; NOW ALSO verified live via new smoke S13 (two
   bookings in one INSERT..SELECT..UNION ALL -> exactly 2 ack rows)
   and boundary negatives via S14 (completed advisory and future
   advisory -> zero ack rows). PASS on the server.
3. Header/comments polish: REVISION v6.1 note appended to the v6
   block (review-pass record); 8g comment clarified (R6 line-number
   caveat "locate by trigger name", b.is_deleted fail-fast nuance);
   rollback header now names the v6 trigger in its drop list.
4. SELF-DETECTED ERROR (fixed before final run): Msg 1046 "Subqueries
   are not allowed in this context" - the S13 FAIL message used
   CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) ...) AS VARCHAR(10)), and T-SQL does not
   allow a subquery as a CAST argument. Fixed by reading the count
   into @ack_count first (DECLARE extended), then casting the
   variable. Recompile passed.

